## 11. Documentation contradictions and unsupported-claim risks

- **High:** [PROJECT_REVIEW_EVIDENCE.md, §10.3](PROJECT_REVIEW_EVIDENCE.md#103-missing-evidence-register) says separately trained 5/10/15 s models and predictive-feature ablations are unavailable. Fits/score tables now exist in the paused study; finalized evaluation remains unavailable. Correct the inventory/scope in a later authorized documentation change; preserve historical evidence.
- **High:** its §3 historical hierarchy (near line680), §9 “Final project outcome” and the README/FINAL_REPORT/dashboard “final” statements reference the completed original run02. These are numerically correct for that named policy, but not a complete current-work inventory. Add a submission-stage notice distinguishing completed baseline from unfinished study; do not replace 0/14 with the provisional one-event result.
- **Medium:** [README, reproduction section](../README.md#reproduce-the-earlier-recall-oriented-evaluation) sends fitting/report commands to existing `results/final/...` paths. `src/run_experiments.py:run` creates directories with `exist_ok=True` and protects `results/validated`, not every final destination. Copy/pasting can overwrite preserved evidence. Use read-only checks for the demo; any later approved reproduction must use a new destination. No such command was run here.
- **Medium:** [LATENCY_REPORT.md](LATENCY_REPORT.md) has historical timing values (e.g. ELM model-only 0.0055 ms) different from the final onset artifact (0.0106245 ms). They are different saved runs/targets, not automatically contradictory measurements; the standalone report needs explicit run/target provenance on presentation slides. Use the authenticated final target CSV for quoted numbers.
- **Medium:** [DASHBOARD_GUIDE.md](DASHBOARD_GUIDE.md), earlier verification sections, and [DASHBOARD_VERIFICATION.md](DASHBOARD_VERIFICATION.md) preserve three-case/temporary-environment and earlier test counts; the current guide labels these historical, but do not use them as current test evidence. Current single-recording wording and tests are authoritative. The project's own reports quote 76/135/136/149/159-test stages: these are dated/stage-specific outcomes, not proof of a currently green suite.
- **Low:** [MODEL_EVALUATION.md, historical pre-onset wording](MODEL_EVALUATION.md) retains older “genuine pre-onset detection”/lead claims, but an explicit historical warning now qualifies them. [FINAL_REPORT.md, final reconciliation](FINAL_REPORT.md#final-evaluation-alarm-budget-experiment) correctly distinguishes 14/14 reusable positives, 13/14 recall-policy one-to-one ELM and 0/14 budget-policy detections. Extracting the old subsection alone would be misleading.
- [RELIABILITY_AUDIT.md, next experiment](RELIABILITY_AUDIT.md) recommends an untouched independent-patient cohort; [LOCAL_30_RECORDING_EVALUATION.md](LOCAL_30_RECORDING_EVALUATION.md) explicitly supersedes acquisition for this local-30 study. No new data is needed/authorized for the present submission.
- No reviewed current safety panel claims clinical readiness, oxygen dosing or demonstrated PID superiority. [PROJECT_REVIEW_EVIDENCE.md, §7/§9](PROJECT_REVIEW_EVIDENCE.md) and [signal_studies/REPORT.md, Study2](../signal_studies/REPORT.md) appropriately limit simulations. A proposed predictive feedforward-PID architecture is not an implemented, validated combined oxygen controller. Novelty and external scientific priority were NOT VERIFIED by a literature search.

