## 13. Ranked blockers

- **Critical if claimed as a working medical system:** no useful final early warning, no oxygen/control benefit evidence and no clinical readiness. Resolve by truthful research framing, not a favorable isolated demo or threshold tuning.
- **High submission:** paused newer study has no finalized manifest/report/uncertainty/timing. Explicitly exclude it from completed claims or authorize a separate bounded completion later. No completion was attempted here.
- **High submission:** stale current-evidence inventory and unqualified “final” chronology. Supply a clear run/target/policy map and disclose red preservation checks without altering protected hashes.
- **Medium demo:** browser/local launch unverified in this restricted environment; rehearse 335–400 s on the actual machine and verify artifact availability. Current AppTest success is functional evidence only.
- **Medium reproducibility:** local ignored artifact dependency, overwrite-prone reproduction snippets, dataset provenance/citation/terms not established here.
- **Low presentation:** distinguish historical graphs, AP/ROC, event counts, false episodes/starts, compute latency and observed lead; avoid misleading cropped captions.

## 14. Minimum actions before demo and submission

**Before demo:** local browser/launch rehearsal; confirm all saved inputs on that machine; use saved final policy and the verified missed record07 event; show pooled negative results; keep the provisional study out of the demonstration's performance claims. No retraining, new search or UI redesign is needed.

**Before submission:** establish an explicit completed-original-study scope, cross-reference paused work and correct stale inventories in a separate authorized edit; make limitations/test exceptions and run provenance prominent; use immutable input/output receipts and a new-directory reproduction recipe; verify dataset citation/terms; include final-policy tables and clearly historical figure captions. A negative result can be submitted academically; a useful predictive oxygen controller cannot be claimed. Completing the paused study is optional if explicitly excluded, not a prerequisite to submitting the completed negative evaluation.

## 15. Defensible conclusion

The project implements a causal, recording-separated retrospective ML comparison and an offline research dashboard. Its authenticated completed final alert policy detects no eligible events, so high historical recall or fast computation does not demonstrate useful anticipation. The same repeatedly examined 30 recordings, unverified patient independence, 14/15 eligible onsets and three severe-interest events limit inference. Illustrative P/PI/PID plots establish no successful feedforward oxygen control. A professor demo is defensible after local rehearsal when it presents the failure honestly; final submission needs the evidence/scope housekeeping listed above. The paused experiments remain paused.

